{"title":"Subjectwise Test-10 Part Syllabus GATE 2026 CS Digital Logic","fileName":"028_Subjectwise Test-10 Part Syllabus GATE 2026 CS Digital Logic.html","branch":"COMPUTER SCIENCE ENGINEERING","series":"GATE 2026 GATE 2025 Online Test Series Computer Science Engineering","provider":"MADE EASY","duration":5400,"questions":[{"qnum":1,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Given that the largest n-bit binary number requires <em>d</em> digits in decimal representation. Which one of the following relations between <em>n</em> and <em>d</em> is approximately correct?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/11cdd42f8c4edec2ffd86e7d99ead64ce9e1156b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/5b26516dbcd28d7d2be2de3009ec95c6f2416cfa.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/9acc0654550dc93d743e97f988fdbb967db958b4.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/9801157523d03af2f37cf1d406432ac402675396.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/493be0337791a5320c71418c4831868f18c8a6b4.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":2,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Consider the logic circuit shown in the figure below:</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/2408767fae5066df2c29cad424394c9ea64fb367.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>The output <em>F</em> is given by</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/0bd77769b342204feb96d65fb11bb31343b939a4.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/6f2103adcc674f6fd0bcd621e2a722ab333997fa.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/1bd1b068811aaf489cdf9e7ce57e77fe8b32a55d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/b39f42b67020da65366186dd194465f228d26f21.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/7c26f4a19b3c3799005023ccaedda8a38256faea.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":3,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>A function <em>F</em> is to be implemented using a 4 : 1 multiplexer where <em>F</em>(<em>A</em>, <em>B</em>, <em>C</em>) = ΠM(0, 3, 5, 6).</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/77708592615f3a53e8d47cf5cb87f59828ab0ee1.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>Which of the following is not correct?</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/bed02bd165e48d9416a7c3787a8f7eccf0852aa3.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/517b80d3ae3cf83351347897a9cdcb1a593dc72e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> F is output difference function of a full subtractor</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/b088e0d3719ec2fb796fe51da1ca2e943d1806b8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/d7b42805d201342aa88dfb2b1d674794a8245298.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":4,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>A Boolean function <img src=\"/media/922e38f3ced787ca64f3b47b34ab0c2a6117aaa1.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is to be implemented using only 2 × 1 multiplexers, the number of 2 × 1 multiplexers required are ________.</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 12</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 13</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 14</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 15</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(d)<br />\nThe Boolean function F is on 4 variables. To implement 4 variable Boolean function a 16 &times; 1 multiplexer is required.<br />\nTo release 16 &times; 1 MUX, number of 2 &times; 1 multiplexers required are 16 &ndash; 1 = 15.</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":5,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A Boolean function is given as,</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/36ee657e0a9f167e3a31b1a18f11028a60ed0687.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>Then the minimum number of two input NAND gates required to implement this function is ________.</div></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"6","high":"6"},"solution":"<p>6</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/7cd31aad43a604d142246c8cdacfc5d6da726aa1.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":6,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>The final values of <em>Q</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>Q</em><sub>0</sub> respectively after 4 clock pulses, if initial values are 00 in the sequential circuit shown below is:</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/b89118f96b751f545bc9da4c1f7e81ee151aa5e0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 10</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 11</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 00</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 01</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/61ece8bc6522e2b1a63d3785664b4c159b2d5e1a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":7,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>If (504)<em><sub>X</sub></em> in base-<em>X</em> is equal to (2320)<sub>4</sub>. Then what will be the value of base-<em>X</em> (in decimal) ________?</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"6","high":"6"},"solution":"<p>6</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/f7ab2177d03f9ae41d54b5094da756d53c095d27.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":8,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Two functions <em>F</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>F</em><sub>2</sub> are given as;</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/79ed6c7af16434c9c5c8382ffd9bf738455d1ddb.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>The number of Essential Prime Implicants (EPIs) in <em>F</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>F</em><sub>2</sub> are <em>A</em> and <em>B</em>. The value of <img src=\"/media/6cbfd788fd21b78796c5fec61dc93686097a4a32.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is _______.</div></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"1","high":"1"},"solution":"<p>1</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/cbde990c7b188780363ea79d338279f882b0002f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":9,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>The table which shows the necessary levels at <em>J</em> and <em>K</em> inputs to produce every possible flip-flop state transition is called</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Truth table (<em>J</em>-<em>K</em>)</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> State transition table (<em>J</em>-<em>K</em>)</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> Excitation table (<em>J</em>-<em>K</em>)</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> None of these</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\nThe excitation table of the flip-flop shows the required excitation to the flip-flop, or the required<br />\ninput to the flip-flop, to go from the given state to the next particular state.</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":10,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A 4-bit ripple counter uses <em>J</em>-<em>K</em> flip-flops. If propagation delay of each flip-flop is 20 nsec, then the maximum clock frequency that can be used is ________ MHz.</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"12.5","high":"12.5"},"solution":"<p>12.5 [12.0 - 13.0]</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/33500f22992a1d017914a324c5e25380bc598b3c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":11,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider the logical function given below:</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/8bf8d48df9de3cdcf316f387c370250be1cd03b7.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>If ‘<em>f</em><sub>out</sub>’ is logic zero, the maximum number of possible minterms of function <em>f</em><sub>3</sub>(<em>A</em>, <em>B</em>, <em>C</em>) is equal to _______.</div></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"6","high":"6"},"solution":"<p>6</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/148fe654355e7c0bb87ca96935b04ea0ead642b6.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":12,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>Which of the following gives the correct simplification of the Boolean expressions?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/6fbf65bf38cf821a889a1f7d6729653d99a9645e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/0503f1ed4f85ef9eb32262470fdbe305f9b35303.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/685a103d69ab188057c5db18278a190334a43f7d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/1bd8c8116c4a8ceebff2770e40103b6a963f6695.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/1697e7899a12fb7c896168e6884feb2f1210db03.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":13,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>The realisation of a combinational logic block as shown in figure to obtain the following truth table involves</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/396e03ba3db7a63c157c738b206bd5545951836a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> NOT and EX-OR gate.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> NOT and EX-NOR gate.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> OR and NAND gate.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> Only EX-OR gates.</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/69d6308a0bb2e271f8eb492ef3f82548e2517ae8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/c33e0d6d8cde6d7899dc217ab105bef4a6ad9848.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":14,"type":"MSQ","correct":"B,C","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>For the circuit below, which of the following options correctly represents <em>f</em>(<em>x</em>, <em>y</em>, <em>z</em>)?</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/712d012f8ee9ef37136236e1b2fcc46301cc4491.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/1bbe2c42c5db9930700eac336afb8b83eb14e447.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/63a3f424086579995de4207fdf2975e65fcb5fd2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/51e8664ba368755110f0f7fe33d147364036680c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/bc1b2966c0f5a99ab9b212d010b46d236fca9727.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b, c)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/b8578ab1f47b0b96d3f4ad278b43775c0d60b536.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n</div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/29042adc0b40e67aa0e465ef3300d3c8b029486f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":15,"type":"NAT","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A 5-bit shift register circuit configured for right-shift operation, i.e., <em>D</em><sub>in</sub> → <em>A</em>, <em>A</em> → <em>B</em>, <em>B</em> → <em>C</em>, <em>C</em> → <em>D</em>, <em>D</em> → <em>E</em> is shown. If the present state of the shift register is <em>ABCDE</em> = 10110, the number of clock cycles required to reach the state <em>ABCDE</em> = 11111 is _______.</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/91060cae8d0e03ce3956ffbb0a230fd558ff9784.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"4","high":"4"},"solution":"<p>4</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/17c3c40250f83f593e0a5e9733aa81861e1abe91.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":16,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>Given below is a synchronous sequential circuit with two <em>T</em> flip-flops <em>T<sub>A</sub></em> and <em>T<sub>B</sub></em> with their outputs denoted as <em>A</em> and <em>B</em> respectively, with <img src=\"/media/b94e8de82c3e43cbd7ee0b50fa842dd0c6a16717.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/d05c32913834c04fa6d164fae0da812de40f34ae.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>Starting from initial state (<em>AB</em> = 00), the sequence of states visited by the circuit is</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 00 → 10 → 01 → 11 → 00</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 00 → 10 → 01 → 11 → 10</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 00 → 01 → 11 → 00</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 00 → 01 → 10 → 11 → 00</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/a953f8a0f49b5fffc9b0cd75bc340c37664d74d9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":17,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,C","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>The below logic expression is to be realized using either two-input NAND Gates or two input NOR Gates:</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/617d7960cfdadfc6058025911e6f15d1f9ecc1ed.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>Which of the following statements is/are correct?</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Number of two-input NAND gates required are 5.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> Number of two-input NOR gates required are 3.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> Number of two-input NOR gates required are 5.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> Number of two-input NAND gates required are 4.</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a, c)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/6ab01c12ab369265bcf3e265d410bb3771ebd91f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":18,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>For a flip-flop with provisions for preset and clear, which of the following options is correct?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Preset and clear operations are performed simultaneously</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> While presetting, clear is disabled.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> While clearing, preset is disabled.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> Both (b) and (c) are true.</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(d)<br />\nThe preset input drives the flip-flop to a set state while the clear input drives it to a reset state.<br />\nHence, both are disabled or only one is enabled at a time.</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":19,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>In the circuit shown below <em>A</em>, <em>B</em>, <em>C</em> are the inputs and <em>P</em>, <em>Q</em> are the two outputs. The circuit is a</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/b115b9c672fee9405fd54f24d4453d6b0accfcb0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Half subtractor where <em>Q</em> is the subtracted value and <em>P</em> is the borrow.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> Full subtractor where <em>Q</em> is the borrow and <em>P</em> is the subtracted value.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> Full adder where <em>Q</em> is the sum and <em>P</em> is the carry.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> Full adder where <em>P</em> is the sum and <em>Q</em> is the carry.</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/4714230b4f781fd88e6441837e9af21d2cff4165.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":20,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>The decimal number 3.248 × 104 is represented in a single precision floating point binary number as</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 1 01101011 11110110100100000000000</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 0 01100010 00001000001000100111111</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 0 10001101 11111011100000000000000</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 1 10001101 111110111000000000000000</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/63f7f5b95198387541eb9bcfd7916b2e711074bc.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":21,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider a 4-bit number <em>A</em> and 2-bit number <em>B</em> are given to a multiplier. The output of multiplier is realized using AND gate and one bit full adders. If minimum number of AND gates required are X and one bit full adders required are <em>Y</em>, then <em>X</em> – <em>Y</em> = _____.</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"4","high":"4"},"solution":"<p>4</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/f6032cf801ca9b8f6e0be2c6184de303f7bc468a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","su